                                "example_id": "0c242fde-cfad-40b1-b886-0cc1770b1480",
                                "sense_id": "a2c5f79a-21a2-3b58-be6c-6ff31d795818",
                                "text": "Descending to the office to buy some postcards, the boys found, lounging about the desk, a stoutish man with a rather dissipated face, puffy under the eyes and heavy about the jaws."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6e83fe4-7479-4892-9d61-6fd7d4e7e690",
                                "sense_id": "a2c5f79a-21a2-3b58-be6c-6ff31d795818",
                                "text": "I joined all my fishing-lines together with stems of seaweed and things, and made a stoutish string, perhaps twelve yards in length or more, and I fastened two lumps of coral rock to the ends of this."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9986e2f-b262-491e-9314-b6e5d50486c9",
                                "sense_id": "a2c5f79a-21a2-3b58-be6c-6ff31d795818",
                                "text": "In the meantime the captain, whom I had observed to be wonderfully swollen about the chest and pockets, had turned out a great many various stores--the British colours, a Bible, a coil of stoutish rope, pen, ink, the log-book, and pounds of tobacco."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
